    "text": "To determine how many miles the car will travel in the next 3 hours, we first need to find the car's speed. The car traveled 180 miles in 4 hours, so we can calculate the speed as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}} = \\frac{180 \\text{ miles}}{4 \\text{ hours}} = 45 \\text{ miles per hour}\n\\]\n\nNow that we know the car's speed is 45 miles per hour, we can calculate how many miles it will travel in the next 3 hours. We do this by multiplying the speed by the time:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance} = \\text{Speed} \\times \\text{Time} = 45 \\text{ miles per hour} \\times 3 \\text{ hours} = 135 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the car will travel \\(\\boxed{135}\\) miles further in the next 3 hours.",
